ink" href="/encyclopedia/fructuosus-of-tarragona">Fructuosus</a> is martyred in the amphitheatre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarraco">Tarraco</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 293</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a> splits off Gallaecia and Carthaginiensis</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">449</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagaudae">Bagaudae</a> and Suebi plunder the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 472–475</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euric">Euric</a> take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarraco">Tarraco</a></span></li></ol>
